brief: '--not-a-declared-flag' is not a flag brief declares. Declared: --help, --home, --instant, --instants-dir, --porcelain. Refused, not ignored: a parser that accepts what no spec declares is a second, hand-maintained copy of the flag list.
fleet brief --instant <value>
    what a dispatched instant needs to know about itself: coordinator, milestone, phase, gate, where its next report will land, and what is outstanding
    --instant <value>            (required) the instant to brief; use `.` from inside it
    --home <value>               the record/pool store root; overrides $FLEET_HOME
    --instants-dir <value>       where instants live; overrides $FLEET_INSTANTS
    --porcelain                  machine form on stdout: tab-separated, no banner (NFR2-7)
    --help                       print this verb's derived usage and exit 0

exit codes:
    0  ok
    1  needs attention / check failed
    2  bad input
    3  no capacity
    4  refused by an admission rule
    pane-guard only (FD-10):
    0  safe
    10 queued-text
    11 mid-turn
    12 not-claude
    13 unknown-pane

